      "dateCreated": "2026-09-28",
      "description": "AptaSelect identifies high-frequency aptamer candidate sequences from paired-end SELEX FASTQ files. Each read (R1 and R2 separately) passes three sequential filters: Stage 1 keeps reads carrying both constant regions (LCR and RCR) within a configurable edit distance, checking the read and then its reverse complement; Stage 2 extracts the sequence between exact inner markers of the constant regions; Stage 3 extracts the random region of exact configurable length between the two stems. Raw reads and each stage are aggregated into count-ranked tables (stable sort, ties in first-seen order), and a survival summary tracks stagewise enrichment. All sequences, tolerances and lengths are configurable so the pipeline can be reused for different library designs.",
